{
  "status": "verified cartoon cross-section subunit; full Phase 3.1 remains open",
  "owner": "Phase 3.1",
  "source": "3ede0e0f + cartoon profile working tree",
  "implementation": [
    "One authoritative CartoonProfile enum is exposed through Rust facade, portable scene specifications, core descriptions, commands, Python keywords/stubs and WASM contracts. Helix defaults to elliptical and nucleic backbone to square, following the specified Mol* defaults.",
    "One fixed sixteen-lane cross-section implementation supplies swept shells and end caps; rounded is a stadium with true semicircular ends and square uses independent planar-face normals.",
    "Source guide kind distinguishes C-alpha protein guides from C4-prime sugar guides. Mixed guide kinds split traces; nucleic physical width/aspect are retained for every profile.",
    "Profile variants enter the persistent ribbon cache key. Editing a profile refreshes geometry/deformation uploads without rewriting the immutable coordinate asset.",
    "A new geometric winding regression exposed inward body triangles; shell triangle winding now agrees with outward vertex normals, including flat twister shells."
  ],
  "complexity": "O(guides + samples) time and memory during geometry preparation; O(1) section evaluation per vertex; unchanged instanced rendering and 32-byte vertex/deformation layouts. Existing reusable vectors retain capacity.",
